narrative:
The Salt Road is choked with wagons and raised voices. At the toll gate, a merchant pushes a fistful of stamped guild scrip across the table. The crown clerk refuses it.

@Merchant: Coin is leaving the road faster than grain. This is what we have.
@Clerk: Then this is what you owe. Standard tender, or turn around.

Nobody is drawing steel. Not yet.

